# AGENTS.md

Guidance for coding agents working in `{{ project_name }}`. `CLAUDE.md` imports this file.

## Project

{{ description }}. The package is `{{ package_name }}`, for Python {{ python_version }}+. The only
runtime dependency is `redis`. `uv` is the only required tool: never use pip, virtualenv
activation, or make.

## Commands

- Install or refresh the environment: `uv sync`
- Run the demo: `uv run {{ project_name }}` (set `REDIS_URL` to use Redis)
- Test: `uv run pytest`
- Lint: `uv run ruff check .`
- Format: `uv run ruff format .` (check only: `uv run ruff format --check .`)
- Type-check: `uv run mypy {{ package_name }} tests`

## Layout

- `{{ package_name }}/jobs.py`: `Job` (a dataclass) and `DeadLetter`.
- `{{ package_name }}/queues.py`: the `Queue` protocol and the in-memory `MemoryQueue`.
- `{{ package_name }}/redis_queue.py`: `RedisQueue`, the Redis implementation of the same protocol.
- `{{ package_name }}/worker.py`: the worker loop, `WorkerConfig`, and signal handling.
- `{{ package_name }}/handlers.py`: example handlers; each validates its untrusted payload.
- `{{ package_name }}/settings.py`: reads `REDIS_URL`. Never log or print the value.
- `{{ package_name }}/app.py`: the demo entry point.
- `tests/`: pytest suite. Worker tests use `MemoryQueue`; Redis tests use `fakeredis`. No test
  contacts a real Redis server, and no sleep is longer than 0.1 seconds.
- `CHANGELOG.md`: add an entry under "Unreleased" for every user-visible change.

## Conventions

- Type-annotate everything, including tests; mypy runs in strict mode and must stay clean.
- Job payloads are untrusted input. Validate every field in a handler before use.
- `REDIS_URL` may hold a password. Never log it, print it, or put it in an error message.
- Never log a payload, and never put a secret in an exception message.
- Keep new runtime dependencies out unless they are clearly needed; ask before adding one.

## Testing

- Add or update tests with every behavior change, including the failure path.
- Inject small backoff values rather than sleeping; keep every test offline.
- Before reporting work as done, run the test, lint, format, and type-check commands above and report
  the real results.

## Safety

- Never read, print, or commit `.env` files, tokens, or other secrets.
- Do not change dependency version bounds without asking first.
- Prefer small, reviewable diffs.
